You promptly roll up something like a torch from dry reed. Doyle cracks the flint and a tongue of flame appears from his fist. Together you come out in front of the savages. They immediately stop dancing and aim tips of spears at you, but when they see waving flame above Doyle's hand, spears begin to shiver. Some savages instantly fall on their knees, and begin to mumble something, lifting up their hands.
"Grol nuktauru! Trort ugga!" at first Doyle's voice trembles, but then he pulls himself together and pronounces this gibberish quite menacingly.
You don't know what that means, but feel that it takes effect upon savages. You bring the torch to the lighter, bright fire blazes up, illuminating frightened painted faces. One of the natives try to look brave. He has a high headwear of motley bird feathers, evidently this is the chief of the tribe or the shaman.
"Kumanu kom!" imperiously says Doyle.
The Chief slowly comes to you, without taking eyes off the flame. You give him the torch, and he accepts it by slightly shaking hand. He could hardly believe the flame was real.
"Ugga!" shouts the chief, lifting the torch high. "Ugga nok!"
"Ugga!" echo his fellow tribesmen.
"Rezhak dadd!" drowning yells of the natives, thunderously heralds Doyle, pointing at Snoopy.
A few savages rush up the cage, get Snoopy and drag him by the rope to you. You understood that Doyle requested due sacrifice. Finally, Snoopy is near. He yelps and tries to lick you in the nose, by shaking hands you try to calm him down. The savages that brought Snoopy, promptly run back and kneel. Only the chief remain standing. He looks with gratitude at the torch in his hand, and his eyes do shine with happiness.    